> [N]ortheast Vietnam has a cool[ to] cold[ season (]courtesy of the northeast monsoon from November[ to March) and a warm to] hot wet[ season (]from April[ to October).] December and[ January in particular can get quite] frost[y in the] far north of Vietnam - pack accordingly. This[ time of the year can also see heavy] mists that[ can run] for[ days] - these can reduce visibility in places like Sapa and Ha Long Bay to frustratingly short distances.[ The] wett[est months of the year in] Hanoi[ are July] and[ August, the] dri[est,] December and[ January.]

